nd volcanoes, with the Moon still orbiting Earth half as far as it is today, appearing 2.8 times larger and producing strong tides.[61]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArchean.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Red_Giant_Earth_warm.jpg/500px-Red_Giant_Earth_warm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Red_Giant_Earth_warm.jpg/500px-Red_Giant_Earth_warm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A conception of the scorched Earth after the Sun has entered the red giant phase, about 5–7 billion years in the future","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Giant_Earth_warm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png/500px-Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png/500px-Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Earth depicted to scale alongside the planetary-mass objects of the Inner Solar System. From left: Mercury, Venus, Earth, the Moon, Mars and Ceres.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATerrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Earth_heat_flow.jpg/500px-Earth_heat_flow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Earth_heat_flow.jpg/500px-Earth_heat_flow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of heat flow from Earth's interior to the surface of Earth's crust, mostly along the oceanic ridges","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth_heat_flow.jpg"}],"sounds":{"earth":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/En-uk-earth.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6f/En-uk-earth.ogg/En-uk-earth.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/En-us-earth.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ad/En-us-earth.ogg/En-us-earth.ogg.mp3"}],"crust":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crust.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/05/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crust.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crust.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/05/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crust.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-crust.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Vase with lamps, Brown and beige textures, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5049019607843137,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vase_with_lamps,_Brown_and_beige_textures,_Rostov-on-Don,_Russia.jpg","share":0.1225},{"title":"Brown ornaments on doors, Reflections, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Brown_ornaments_on_doors%2C_Reflections%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Brown_ornaments_on_doors%2C_Reflections%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5,"li